Track 2: Magnetic Stripe Erosion
- Story & Context: Beneath the shifting sands of the Obsidian Dunes, Elias, a former data archivist, unearthed a heavily corroded magnetic data tape, its fragile stripe flickering with fragmented, ghostly piano notes that spoke of a civilization lost to solar flares and cosmic radiation. He wept as he listened, knowing the memories encoded within were disintegrating, mirroring the slow, mechanical decay of his own heart, powered by a crudely integrated clockwork bypass pump. "My ghost data still hums its grief," he rasped, clutching the relic tight.
